&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an HR Generalist to join our team. You will be a key partner working in a fast-paced environment across various business units, with the goal of enhancing and simplifying how our teams engage with HR support and policy compliance. This role offers a real opportunity for significant development and direct exposure to all aspects of the HR function—from talent acquisition and performance management to compensation and employee relations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are looking for a smart individual who wants to do more than just manage, but also shape and innovate!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will have the opportunity to (your tasks):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the first point of contact for client groups; address and resolve requests, concerns and inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and escalate employee issues that arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze HR data to provide insights to the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support monthly payroll processing by tracking employee-related changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate the local implementation of global programmes to drive the desired culture and improve employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating the recruiting process in Germany&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide current and prospective employees with information about policies, working conditions, and employee benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support benefit application and benefit enrollment and handle associated correspondence in partnership with the global reward team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate and communicate organizational policies, and recommended best practices to maintain compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key role in the onboarding and offboarding of employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are some of the things you&#39;ll bring (requirements):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires a Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 2 years of human resources experience, preferably in a generalist role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of German employment law, knowledge of additional EMEA jurisdictions is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The position requires a self-starter with excellent problem analysis/resolution, employee relations, and customer service skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to effectively build and leverage professional relationships and work well within a team approach environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal, presentation, verbal and written communication skills are a must.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good command of German and English is essential, additional European languages a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of accuracy, detail orientation and strong computer skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possessing talent acquisition experience is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well independently, as needed, with limited supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that the successful candidate for this role must live within a commutable distance of Mannheim.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
