&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Timings: 1.30 PM IST to 10.30 PM IST&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LivePerson (NASDAQ: LPSN) is a leader in trusted enterprise conversational AI and digital transformation. The world&#39;s leading brands use our award-winning Conversational Cloud platform to connect with millions of consumers. We power nearly a billion conversational interactions every month, providing uniquely rich data analytics and safety tools to unlock the power of conversational AI for better business outcomes. Fast Company named LivePerson the #1 Most Innovative AI Company in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a passionate QA professional who enjoys ensuring product quality across both user-facing experiences and backend systems? We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;QA Engineer II&lt;/strong&gt; to play a key role in delivering high-quality releases through strong manual testing practices, thoughtful risk-based testing, and close cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work across web and mobile platforms, validating both UI and Backend functionality through comprehensive test planning, structured exploratory testing, API validation, and workflow/data integrity checks. You will partner closely with Product and Engineering teams to improve requirement clarity, strengthen testability early in the development lifecycle, and help drive release confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will primarily support teams working in the &lt;strong&gt;EU and US time zones&lt;/strong&gt;, and the expected working hours are approximately 1&lt;strong&gt;:30 PM to 10:30 PM IST&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity for someone detail-oriented, proactive, and excited to contribute not only to day-to-day test execution, but also to the continuous improvement of QA processes and the broader quality culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute comprehensive test plans and test cases for both UI and Backend components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform UI testing across web and mobile platforms, including functional, regression, smoke, and exploratory testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Backend testing, including API validation, microservices testing, workflow verification, and data integrity checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead structured exploratory testing sessions to uncover edge cases, usability concerns, and high-risk defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review user stories and acceptance criteria to ensure clarity, completeness, and testability before development begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply risk-based testing principles to prioritise critical functionality, high-risk edge cases, complex integrations, and areas with a higher impact of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product and Engineering teams to identify requirement gaps early and improve overall product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, document, and track defects with clear reproduction steps, expected/actual behaviour, and supporting evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with developers and stakeholders to support timely defect triage and resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate actively in test planning, estimation, and test coverage discussions to support release readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of test progress, results, and coverage metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of quality for assigned product areas and contribute to release readiness and go/no-go recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving QA processes, standards, and best practices across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support efforts to increase automated test coverage across UI and Backend areas in collaboration with automation-focused team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date with QA tools, testing trends, and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your qualifications are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of QA methodologies, &lt;strong&gt;test strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;test coverage principles&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;risk-based testing&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to review &lt;strong&gt;user stories and acceptance criteria&lt;/strong&gt;, identify ambiguities/gaps, and improve &lt;strong&gt;testability&lt;/strong&gt; early in the development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clear, high-quality &lt;strong&gt;test plans, test cases, and exploratory test charters&lt;/strong&gt;, and to document defects with reproducible steps, expected vs. actual behavior, and supporting evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with &lt;strong&gt;Product, Engineering, and QA&lt;/strong&gt; teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset with the ability to manage quality for assigned product areas and contribute to &lt;strong&gt;QA process improvements&lt;/strong&gt; and team best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to mentor junior QA team members and support a culture of continuous learning and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of &lt;strong&gt;test automation concepts&lt;/strong&gt; and interest in supporting automation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field preferred. Candidates with strong relevant QA experience in place of a formal technical degree are also encouraged to apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Have Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years of hands-on QA experience&lt;/strong&gt; in manual testing across &lt;strong&gt;UI and Backend systems&lt;/strong&gt; (web/mobile + backend services), including strong &lt;strong&gt;test planning, test design, and execution&lt;/strong&gt; skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience in &lt;strong&gt;functional, regression, smoke, negative, and exploratory testing&lt;/strong&gt;, with hands-on &lt;strong&gt;API/Backend testing&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Postman&lt;/strong&gt;) and working knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;basic SQL / data validation&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using &lt;strong&gt;defect/test management tools&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Jira&lt;/strong&gt;) and contributing to &lt;strong&gt;test coverage discussions, test estimation, and release readiness / go-no-go recommendations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;analytical thinking, problem-solving ability, and attention to detail&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to work effectively in a cross-functional product development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good to Have Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ISTQB &lt;/strong&gt;(or equivalent) certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automation tools such as&lt;strong&gt; Playwright, Cypress, Nightwatch, or Selenium.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with&lt;strong&gt; CI/CD systems (e.g., GitLab).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;Java or JavaScript.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal time off 15 days - Casual (6) days &amp;amp; Sick Days (6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical Insurance: 8 Lakhs Family Floater that covers employee, spouse, 3 children and parents or In-laws&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group Personal Accident: 3x of the employee’s Gross Salary&lt;/li&gt;
